\pard\sb180\sa90\b\fs24 4. Purpose\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa120 NutManager may be used, among other things, to:\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab monitor NUT servers and UPS units;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab inspect state, load, battery and other information published by NUT;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab manage server profiles;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab edit NUT configuration through a graphical interface;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab generate previews before changes are applied;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab back up, validate, safely replace and roll back configuration;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab inspect and administer the Windows service associated with NUT;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab list available serial ports;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab use NutManager Agent for authorised remote administration;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab run diagnostics related to the NUT environment.\par
\pard\sa120 The features actually available may vary with version, environment, permissions, hardware, operating system and NUT configuration.\par
\pard\sb180\sa90\b\fs24 5. Administrator responsibility\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa120 NutManager is an administrative tool. Some operations can directly affect the availability of the power monitoring system.\par
\pard\sa120 The user is responsible for:\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab understanding changes before applying them;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab reviewing the preview the software presents;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab keeping adequate backups;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab ensuring they are authorised to administer the computers involved;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab keeping credentials, certificates and access keys protected;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab confirming that configuration is compatible with their hardware and their version of NUT;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab testing changes in a suitable environment when necessary;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab assessing the impact before stopping or restarting services.\par
\pard\sa120 \b Interrupting the NUT service can interrupt UPS monitoring and the automatic shutdown mechanisms associated with power failures.\b0 \par
\pard\sb180\sa90\b\fs24 6. Configuration changes\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa120 NutManager uses mechanisms intended to reduce the risk of file corruption, including:\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab validation;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab a preview before writing;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab backup;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab temporary write;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab safe replacement;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab verification afterwards;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab rollback where applicable.\par
\pard\sa120 These mechanisms reduce risk, but \b do not guarantee that every change will produce the intended behaviour in NUT or in the connected hardware\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120 The user remains responsible for the content and the consequences of the configuration applied.\par
\pard\sa120 NutManager deliberately \b does not automatically restart NUT after a configuration change\b0 . Where that is needed, the administrator must perform it separately.\par
\pard\sb180\sa90\b\fs24 7. Service control\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa120 NutManager may allow operations such as:\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab start;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab stop;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab restart;\par
\pard\sa120 on the Windows service related to NUT.\par
\pard\sa120 These operations can cause temporary or permanent loss of monitoring.\par
\pard\sa120 The user should assess the impact before performing them.\par
\pard\sb180\sa90\b\fs24 8. NutManager Agent\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa120 \b NutManager Agent\b0  is an optional component intended for administering remote Windows servers.\par
\pard\sa120 The Agent:\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab operates under the permissions configured on the server;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab uses Windows authentication mechanisms;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab restricts administrative operations to authorised users;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab does not act as a general-purpose remote execution mechanism;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab must not be treated as a substitute for the organisation's security policies.\par
\pard\sa120 It is the administrator's responsibility to correctly configure:\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab the NutManager Operators group;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab permissions;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab certificates;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab HTTPS, where used;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab the firewall;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab Windows policies;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab authorised credentials.\par
\pard\sb180\sa90\b\fs24 9. Credentials and security\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa120 Certain features may use credentials for:\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab SFTP;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab SMB;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab NutManager Agent;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab NUT authentication.\par
\pard\sa120 Where supported, NutManager may use the \b Windows Credential Manager\b0  to store credentials.\par
\pard\sa120 The user is responsible for:\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab protecting their Windows account;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab limiting administrative access to the machine;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab protecting private keys;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab using valid certificates;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab controlling who belongs to the authorised groups;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab removing credentials once they are no longer needed.\par
\pard\sa120 No credential storage mechanism should be considered absolute protection against the compromise of a machine already controlled by an attacker.\par
\pard\sb180\sa90\b\fs24 10. Privacy and telemetry\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa120 The current version of NutManager \b has no telemetry system and performs no automatic collection of usage data by the developer\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120 The information the application processes is used locally or transmitted directly to the servers the user has configured, according to the feature being used.\par
\pard\sa120 That may include connections to:\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab a NUT server;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab an SFTP server;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab an SMB share;\par
\pard\fi-200\li480\sa40\bullet\tab NutManager Agent.\par
\pard\sa120 External links, such as GitHub and documentation, are reached only on explicit user action.\par
\pard\sb180\sa90\b\fs24 11. Third-party software and services\b0\fs20\par
